{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"a46014a2f7b89cc33da4acd54806b4a9f0e13634242adc7a62e6a0117a29d60e","digest":{"component_or_area":"rebar reconciler","key_entities":["apply_handlers.py","reconcile.py","RECONCILER_FAIL_SILENT_NOOP","comment_errors","mutation_failures","acli_subprocess._check_mutation_failure","reconcile-bridge.yml","test_silent_noop_canary.py"],"problem_keywords":["silent-no-op","fail-loud","comment_errors","reconciler","exit-code","observability","partial-failure","mutation-failure"],"propositions":["Partial comment failures are swallowed as non-fatal and not counted in mutation_failures, allowing the reconciler to exit with code 0 despite sync failures.","The silent-no-op canary only hard-fails behind RECONCILER_FAIL_SILENT_NOOP flag (default off), so sync failures remain invisible by default.","When comment_errors are present and the RECONCILER_FAIL_SILENT_NOOP flag is enabled, the outcome should be marked as error to count toward mutation_failures and drive non-zero pass exit.","The flag must remain off by default during landing and be activated only after Jira comment cleanup completes to avoid failing passes on still-capped tickets."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787903110362716001,"uuid":"4e8dc2d1-96f9-4d45-a7c0-90c8f01cd8ca"}